Rebased onto main. The conflict was with the `<= 16` SM gate that landed in the meantime.

That check now lives inside the `else` of the import guard, so the chain is byte-for-byte the same whenever flashinfer imports:

```python
try:
    from vllm.v1.attention.backends.flashinfer import FlashInferBackend
except ImportError as exc:
    unsupported_reason = f"FlashInfer is not installed ({exc})"
else:
    if not FlashInferBackend.supports_compute_capability(capability):
        ...
    elif (num_sms := ...) <= 16:
        ...
    else:
        unsupported_reason = _flashinfer_jit_unsupported_reason(capability)
```

Checked on a GB10 (sm_121, 48 SMs, flashinfer 0.6.18.post1): `flashinfer_sampler_supported()` still returns True and logs `Using FlashInfer for top-p & top-k sampling`, i.e. the guard changes nothing where flashinfer is actually importable. 48 > 16 there, if a Blackwell data point is useful for the new SM gate.

